# demo-store — agent context

This is a deliberately broken Next.js storefront. Its purpose is to generate realistic error
traffic for the agentic-triage-demo project. Read this file before making any changes.

## What this repo is

- A Next.js App Router storefront that calls `demo-store-api` as its upstream service
- Bugs are INTENTIONAL — do not fix them unless explicitly asked
- The agentic-triage agent investigates errors in THIS repo's code; it cannot see demo-store-api internals

## Repo layout

```
app/
  (shop)/page.tsx          # Storefront UI — Add to cart, Search, Checkout, Sign in
  api/
    auth/route.ts          # POST — session creation (auth race bug)
    cart/route.ts          # POST — add to cart (null dereference bug)
    checkout/route.ts      # POST — checkout (pricing regression + idempotency bug)
    checkout-price/route.ts# POST — price lookup (price override bug)
    edge/route.ts          # GET  — edge function (missing env var bug, Edge runtime)
    guest-orders/route.ts  # POST — guest order (orphaned session bug)
    health/route.ts        # GET  — health check (noise/no-context bug)
    orders/route.ts        # POST — create order (FK violation bug)
    products/route.ts      # GET  — product list (timeout + rate limit bugs)
    search/route.ts        # GET  — search (silent failure bug)
lib/
  apiFetch.ts              # Shared fetch helper for calls to demo-store-api
  pricing.ts               # applyDiscount() — contains the pricing regression bug
middleware.ts              # Two-layer auth: Basic Auth (all routes) + Bearer/x-e2e-token (cron routes)
e2e/
  generate-errors.spec.ts  # Playwright script that triggers all 12 errors
  playwright.config.ts
  package.json
```

## The 12 errors

| # | File | Line | Bug | Always-on? | Env flag |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | app/api/checkout/route.ts | 12 | Idempotency-Key header never sent to payment API (always-on) | Yes | — |
| 2 | lib/pricing.ts | 5 | discount - subtotalPence instead of subtotalPence - discount (always-on) | Yes | — |
| 3 | app/api/auth/route.ts | 7 | 60ms sleep between session check and write (race window, always-on) | Yes | — |
| 4 | app/api/orders/route.ts | 11 | e2e traffic sends stale productId "prod-3f4a1c" which no longer exists in the map | Yes | — |
| 5 | app/api/edge/route.ts | 4 | Reads REVALIDATION_SECRET which is never set | Yes | — |
| 6 | app/api/health/route.ts | 5 | Discards upstream error body, logs nothing useful | No | FAULT_HEALTH (on demo-store-api) |
| 7 | app/api/search/route.ts | 12 | catch block swallows stack, returns empty results | No | FAULT_SEARCH_SILENT (on demo-store-api) |
| 8 | app/api/cart/route.ts | 8 | cart!.items non-null assertion crashes when cart is undefined (always-on) | Yes | — |
| 9 | app/api/checkout-price/route.ts | 3 | Trusts client-supplied subtotalPence, no server-side lookup (always-on) | Yes | — |
| 10 | app/api/guest-orders/route.ts | 4 | Creates order with sessionId: null then throws (always-on) | Yes | — |
| 11 | app/api/products/route.ts | 6 | No AbortSignal.timeout() — platform 504 when upstream delays 12s | No | FAULT_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT (on demo-store-api) |
| 12 | app/api/products/route.ts | 7 | No 429 handling or retry — crashes on upstream rate limit | No | FAULT_UPSTREAM_RATE_LIMIT (on demo-store-api) |
| 13 | app/api/products/route.ts | 11 | N+1: fires a per-product enrichment call to /api/products/:id which does not exist — 4 upstream 404s per request | Yes | — |

## Auth model

middleware.ts enforces two layers on every request:

  Layer 1 — Basic Auth (all routes):
    Header: Authorization: Basic <base64(BASIC_USER:BASIC_PASS)>
    Only active if BASIC_USER and BASIC_PASS env vars are set.

  Layer 2 — E2E token (cron-only routes only):
    Header: Authorization: Bearer <E2E_TOKEN>
       OR   x-e2e-token: <E2E_TOKEN>
    Only active if E2E_TOKEN env var is set.
    Routes exempt from layer 2 (UI-safe): /api/cart, /api/auth, /api/search, /api/checkout, /api/products

The x-e2e-token header exists so browser-context fetches (which need Authorization for Basic Auth)
can still reach cron-only routes without header conflicts.

## Generating errors

  Via UI buttons:
    Checkout x2 (50ms gap)  → errors #1, #2
    Sign in x2 (50ms gap)   → error #3
    Add to cart             → error #8
    Search form submit      → error #7

  Via Playwright (triggers all 12):
    cd e2e && npm install && npx playwright install chromium && npm run generate-errors

  Via GitHub Actions cron (hourly):
    .github/workflows/e2e.yml — requires STORE_URL and E2E_TOKEN secrets

## Rules for agents working in this repo

1. Do NOT fix the intentional bugs in the error catalogue above.
2. Do NOT remove or weaken the FAULT_* env var checks — they are the on/off switch for each error.
3. Middleware changes must preserve both auth layers and the x-e2e-token escape hatch.
4. The e2e/ directory is standalone (its own package.json) — do not add Playwright to the root package.json.
5. lib/pricing.ts:7 contains the intentional regression — do not "fix" the arithmetic.
6. When adding new intentional errors, follow the same pattern: FAULT_ env var guard, comment
   marking the bug, and a corresponding entry in the e2e Playwright spec.
